; A windtrap suite over the coverage runtime. The runtime's independence
; from the windtrap core is a property of lib/runtime (and pinned by
; test/coverage_ppx/semantics/test_linkonly); the suite itself dogfoods
; windtrap. dump_child is a separate instrumented-like executable
; exercising the at_exit dump end to end, redirected to a scratch file
; via WINDTRAP_COVERAGE_FILE. WINDTRAP_COVERAGE=off keeps the runner's
; inline coverage line out of runtest: the suite's synthetic in-process
; registrations would render a meaningless percentage on every green
; run.
;
; WINDTRAP_COVERAGE_FILE points this executable's OWN at_exit dump at a
; name inside the action's directory, so it never lands in the project's
; _build/_coverage. It is set here rather than by a putenv in the test
; because the destination is resolved at the first registration in the
; process — and under `--instrument-with` that is a windtrap core
; module's, at library load, before any of the test's own code runs.

(executable
 (name dump_child)
 (modules dump_child)
 (libraries windtrap_runtime))

(test
 (name test_coverage)
 (modules test_coverage)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_runtime unix)
 (deps dump_child.exe)
 (action
  (setenv
   WINDTRAP_COVERAGE
   off
   (setenv
    WINDTRAP_COVERAGE_FILE
    test_coverage.coverage
    (run %{test})))))
